thinking:
FOUND IT! The AP's `bk_gpio_driver_init()` has:

```c
//interrupt to CPU enable
#if (CONFIG_SYSTEM_CTRL)
    sys_drv_int_group2_enable(GPIO_INTERRUPT_CTRL_BIT);
#else
    icu_enable_gpio_interrupt();
#endif
```

This is at line 180-184, RIGHT AFTER `bk_int_isr_register()`. The AP enables GPIO source forwarding during normal GPIO init, not just in the low-power path.

Now let me compare CP vs AP:

**CP (`cp/middleware/driver/gpio/gpio_driver_base.c`):**
```c
bk_err_t bk_gpio_driver_init(void)
{
    // ... init code ...
    bk_int_isr_register(INT_SRC_GPIO, gpio_isr, NULL);
    // NO sys_drv_int_group2_enable() here!
    s_gpio_is_init = true;
    return BK_OK;
}
```

The CP version is missing the interrupt enable call entirely, while the AP has it configured to either use the system control driver or fall back to the ICU interrupt enable depending on the CONFIG_SYSTEM_CTRL flag.

Looking at the low-power entry and exit functions, I can see the CP does enable GPIO interrupts during the low-power transition, then disables them when exiting. So the CP is aware of GPIO interrupt handling but only manages it during power state changes, whereas the AP keeps it enabled as part of normal initialization.

The architectural difference is becoming clear: the AP treats GPIO interrupt forwarding as a standard feature that's always active, while the CP treats it as a power-saving optimization that's only active when needed. This explains why NuttX running on the CP doesn't get GPIO interrupts unless we explicitly enable them during our GPIO setup routine.

text:
关键发现！AP 和 CP 的 `bk_gpio_driver_init()` 有本质区别：

**AP（Application Processor）：**
```c
// ap/middleware/driver/gpio/gpio_driver_base.c:179-184
// Move ISR to last to avoid other resouce doesn't finish but isr has came.
bk_int_isr_register(INT_SRC_GPIO, gpio_isr, NULL);

//interrupt to CPU enable          ← 正常初始化中 enable
#if (CONFIG_SYSTEM_CTRL)
    sys_drv_int_group2_enable(GPIO_INTERRUPT_CTRL_BIT);
#else
    icu_enable_gpio_interrupt();
#endif
```

**CP（Communication Processor）：**
```c
// cp/middleware/driver/gpio/gpio_driver_base.c:168-177
bk_int_isr_register(INT_SRC_GPIO, gpio_isr, NULL);
// ← 没有 source enable！
s_gpio_is_init = true;
return BK_OK;
```

CP 只在 `gpio_enter_low_power()` 中 enable，AP 在正常 init 中就 enable。

**原因**：CP 设计为低功耗核心，GPIO 中断转发只在进入低功耗时才开启，平时关闭以省电。AP 作为主处理器，GPIO 中断始终开启。

**结论**：我们做的是 NuttX 在 CP 核心上的桥接层。既然 CP 的 GPIO 驱动不在正常 init 中 enable source forwarding，我们需要在 NuttX 的 GPIO 初始化路径中自己调用。用 `extern` 声明 `sys_drv_int_group2_enable()` 是正确的，因为这个符号在 CP 的 `libdriver.a` 中存在且已板端验证。

